{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "nr-lawn-garden-county",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7e: the `nr-lawn-garden-county` RunSpec computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE -- Washtenaw County, August 2020, weekday, the Lawn/Garden sector, gasoline, THC, CO, NOx and PM10. The second rung, and the first nonroad run here with no fixture behind it: 97 equipment points over 31 SCCs, 484 cohorts, 1,936 rows.\n\nIT FOUND TWO LOOKUP RULES THE FIRST RUN COULD NOT TELL APART. Five of its SCCs came out wrong, from 0.002 % to 86 %, with every key right. Three were NONROAD's SCC chain walked per (pollutant, technology) rather than per point: 2265004076's exact rows rate hp 0 to 6 and nothing above, so its bigger points read the equipment root for some technologies and nothing for others. The other two were a point ON a bin boundary -- 2260004071 at 3.0 hp, between [1, 3] and [3, 6] -- which NONROAD reads from the lower bin and the fixture's filter read from both. With both rules all 1,936 rows reproduce at 6.718e-06."
  },
